1543..1614 Comment "/// Spinning a sum is composing the spins (cubical\'s `intLoop-hom`), by"
1615..1688 Comment "/// induction on the second summand. `spin` puts its new loop first where"
1689..1766 Comment "/// cubical\'s `intLoop` puts it last, so the law composes the spins the other"
1767..1833 Comment "/// way round, as the words compute: `Path.step(loop ∷ p, q)` is"
1834..1910 Comment "/// `loop ∷ Path.step(p, q)`. At zero `spin(Z)` is a call that returns the"
1911..1978 Comment "/// empty word, and the composite over it runs that call first; the"
1979..2043 Comment "/// composites the arms carry convert through their definitions."
