2311..2388 Comment "/// Winding a composite is summing the windings (cubical\'s `winding-hom`), by"
2389..2463 Comment "/// induction on the first loop, written last so its match stands directly"
2464..2542 Comment "/// under the recursion, where the checkers read it as a fold, and summed with"
2543..2607 Comment "/// `wind(q)` first because the sum descends its second summand:"
2608..2688 Comment "/// `Path.here(wind(q))` on the empty word, and the recursive call carried along"
2689..2762 Comment "/// `up` or `down`. The composite in its type is read off the parameters\'"
2763..2815 Comment "/// written types, and the kernel reads its endpoint"
2816..2868 Comment "/// `plus(wind(q), wind(p))` as the call it returns."
